(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #108 aliasing probe: the same `as text` pointer
 pass-through as 573, but through `Set u to src as text.` rather than a
 declaration initializer - the sibling statement kind
 (`Statement::Assignment`'s global branch) that the fix's free-on-`Set`
 machinery also runs through, so it needs its own probe.)

a number called n is 2.
a text called src is "v{n}".
a text called u is "".
Set u to src as text.
Set src to "z{n}".
a number called i is 0.
While i is less than 50, Set src to "q{i}", increment i.
Print "u={u} src={src}".
